  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "The second-degree Taylor polynomial of a function $f(x)$ about $x=-2$ is given by ${P}_{2}(x)=2+4(x+2)+16(x+2)^{2}.$ What is the value of ${f}^{\u2033}(-2)?$",
  "worked_solution": "This is an expansion about the point $x=-2,$ so the coefficient of the second-degree term is $\\frac{1}{2}{f}^{\u2033}(-2).$ \n\nIn the given equation, we see that the coefficient of the second-degree term is $16.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}{f}^{\u2033}(-2)=16\\,\u27f9\\,{f}^{\u2033}(-2)=32.\n$$",
